===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make a noise of metal or glass clattering against itself.
#: {{ux|en|The beads '''jingled''' as she walked.}}
#* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|chapter=IV|page=54|passage=He heard then a warm heavy sigh, softer, as she turned over and the loose brass quoits of the bedstead '''jingled'''. Must get those settled really.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to make a noise of metal or glass clattering against itself.
#: {{ux|en|She '''jingled''' the beads as she walked.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|intransitive}} To [[rhyme]] or [[sound]] with a jingling effect.
#* {{RQ:Macaulay History of England|chapter=15|passage='''jingling''' street ballads}}

